  "ALL_TEXT": "40 INT. AUDITORIUM - DAY \nSUBBA RAJU is performing the \"Navarasas\" on stage. The \nauditorium is pretty empty but for seven eight people, with a \nseat occupied by a serious looking, middle-aged, salt-and \npepper bearded man, film director SHAM GOPAL VERMA. \nHe is watching intently. The camera tilts down to show that \nhis hands are tied. The still silence of the SHAM GOPAL VERMA \nstops when he squirms some words out \nSHAM GOPAL VERMA \nEnti raa ee torture, entha weed \nkotti dorikesta ila kattestaavaa \nSUBBA RAJU \nSir, sir, aipoindi sir, inko oka \nrendu rasaalu \nSHAM GOPAL VERMA(V.O) \n(Frustrated) \nMari adhe aydho cheyyi raa, malli \ncheptaaventi raa geddam maasina \ngamma... \nWhile performing, SUBBA RAJU sees the COMMISSIONER, turns and \nstarts to runs away. He looks at SHAM GOPAL VERMA \nSUBBA RAJU \nMalli sayantram kalustaanu sir \nSHAM GOPAL VERMA \nRei, idem torture raa! Katlu ippi \nellu raa.. \nCUT TO:",
